                <pb facs="0709" n="1669" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1669"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in B.—Extract from the New York Times of
                        August 22, 1883]</seg></opener>
                <p>There is this further consideration in favor of supporting the administration on
                    this issue. It will leave the question still open for friendly means of
                    settlement of some kind, while a support of the Senate’s position would close
                    all avenues of future negotiations and bring upon the country the disastrous
                    consequences of retaliation, hostility, and possible war. It would put an end to
                    all prospect of improving the commercial relations of the United States and
                    Canada. This is one of the questions which the people should keep in mind in
                    casting their votes next November.</p>
            </div>
